### 5.3  Aggregate (Write side)

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/domain/OrderAggregate.java
package com.example.domain;

import org.axonframework.modelling.command.AggregateIdentifier;
import org.axonframework.modelling.command.AggregateLifecycle;
import org.axonframework.modelling.command.Aggregate;
import org.axonframework.modelling.command.CommandHandler;
import org.axonframework.modelling.command.AggregateLifecycle;

@Aggregate
public class OrderAggregate {

    @AggregateIdentifier
    private UUID orderId;
    private String productId;
    private int quantity;

    // Required by Axon
    protected OrderAggregate() {}

    @CommandHandler
    public OrderAggregate(CreateOrderCommand cmd) {
        // Validation
        if (cmd.quantity() <= 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Quantity must be > 0");
        // Persist event
        AggregateLifecycle.apply(new OrderCreatedEvent(cmd.orderId(), cmd.productId(), cmd.quantity()));
    }

    @EventSourcingHandler
    public void on(OrderCreatedEvent evt) {
        this.orderId = evt.orderId();
        this.productId = evt.productId();
        this.quantity = evt.quantity();
    }
}
```

> **Important** – the constructor annotated with `@CommandHandler` **creates** a new aggregate.  
> `AggregateLifecycle.apply()` publishes the event to the event store and to the event bus.

### 5.4  Read Model (Projection)

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/readmodel/OrderReadModel.java
package com.example.readmodel;

import org.axonframework.eventhandling.EventHandler;
import org.axonframework.eventhandling.SourcingEventHandler;
import org.axonframework.eventhandling.EventHandlerConfiguration;
import org.axonframework.eventhandling.EventHandler;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import com.example.domain.OrderCreatedEvent;

import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.UUID;

@Component
public class OrderReadModel {

    private final ConcurrentHashMap<UUID, OrderDto> store = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    @EventHandler
    public void on(OrderCreatedEvent evt) {
        store.put(evt.orderId(), new OrderDto(evt.orderId(), evt.productId(), evt.quantity()));
    }

    public OrderDto find(UUID orderId) {
        return store.get(orderId);
    }

    public Collection<OrderDto> all() {
        return store.values();
    }
}
```

> The event handler runs **asynchronously** on Axon’s default `EventProcessingConfigurer`.  
> For heavy reads you normally persist the projection in a database (JPA, Mongo, Elastic).

### 5.5  Query Handlers

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/query/GetOrderQuery.java
package com.example.query;

import java.util.UUID;
import org.axonframework.queryhandling.Query;

public record GetOrderQuery(UUID orderId) implements Query<OrderDto> {}
```

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/query/GetOrderQueryHandler.java
package com.example.query;

import org.axonframework.queryhandling.QueryHandler;
import org.axonframework.queryhandling.ResultHandler;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import com.example.readmodel.OrderReadModel;
import com.example.readmodel.OrderDto;

@Component
public class GetOrderQueryHandler {

    private final OrderReadModel readModel;

    public GetOrderQueryHandler(OrderReadModel readModel) {
        this.readModel = readModel;
    }

    @QueryHandler
    public OrderDto handle(GetOrderQuery query, ResultHandler<OrderDto> resultHandler) {
        OrderDto dto = readModel.find(query.orderId());
        resultHandler.handleResult(dto);
        return dto;
    }
}
```

### 5.6  Controllers (REST)

```java
// src/main/java/com/example/web/OrderController.java
package com.example.web;

import org.axonframework.commandhandling.gateway.CommandGateway;
import org.axonframework.queryhandling.QueryGateway;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import com.example.domain.CreateOrderCommand;
import com.example.query.GetOrderQuery;
import com.example.readmodel.OrderDto;

import java.util.UUID;
import java.util.concurrent.Future;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/orders")
public class OrderController {

    private final CommandGateway commandGateway;
    private final QueryGateway queryGateway;

    public OrderController(CommandGateway commandGateway, QueryGateway queryGateway) {
        this.commandGateway = commandGateway;
        this.queryGateway = queryGateway;
    }

    @PostMapping
    public UUID create(@RequestBody CreateOrderRequest req) throws Exception {
        UUID id = UUID.randomUUID();
        // Send command synchronously
        commandGateway.sendAndWait(new CreateOrderCommand(id, req.productId(), req.quantity()));
        return id;
    }

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public OrderDto get(@PathVariable UUID id) throws Exception {
        Future<OrderDto> future = queryGateway.query(new GetOrderQuery(id), OrderDto.class);
        return future.get(); // block for demo
    }
}

class CreateOrderRequest {
    public String productId;
    public int quantity;
}
```

### 5.7  Running

* `mvn spring-boot:run`  
* POST `/orders` → returns a UUID.  
* GET `/orders/{id}` → returns the read‑model DTO.

**Behind the scenes**

1. `CommandGateway.sendAndWait()` dispatches `CreateOrderCommand` → `OrderAggregate` → `OrderCreatedEvent`.
2. Axon stores the event (default H2 event store).
3. Event bus routes `OrderCreatedEvent` → `OrderReadModel` → projection update.
4. `QueryGateway.query()` asks `GetOrderQueryHandler`, which fetches from `OrderReadModel`.

